From 343b5058f7e164b6f1bf2454a47ee7fc482aae6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luc3as <luc3as@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 20:19:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/25] A mark of its own: a coat hanger whose hook is a target
 ring
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous mark — a price tag in a reticle — was generic and its wordmark
depended on whatever sans-serif the reader's machine had. Replaced with an
identity that says what the tool is about in one shape: a coat hanger (the
market) whose hook is a target ring (the sniper). The same hanger inside a
scope serves as icon and favicon; on the accent colour it works as an app or
bot avatar. The wordmark sets "vinted" light and "sniper" bold in Outfit
(OFL) converted to paths, so it renders identically everywhere, with the
tagline "watch · judge · pounce". Light and dark colourways, PNG renders for
places that cannot take SVG. The dashboard header carries the mark drawn
with currentColor and the accent token, so it follows the theme.

The logo files carry their own licence — all rights reserved to the fork
owner — separate from the code's MIT; docs/media/logo/LICENSE.md and the
README say so. Nothing in the mark derives from any marketplace's branding.
